            <ArticleTitle>Acute abdominal pain in childhood. Finding the cause.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>119-21, 124-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The child with acute abdominal pain poses a problem of differential diagnosis. Selection of diagnostic studies and initial management depends on the unique characteristics of history or physical examination that narrow the range of possible underlying causes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
